{"duration_api_ms":234450,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"dd2c2f99-a5c8-4e0f-9d7a-f1c8078ca1e4","total_cost_usd":1.2226004000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59691,"cache_read_input_tokens":3817817,"output_tokens":21583,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2647},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59691,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2872,"cache_read_input_tokens":75761,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4091,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004171,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":136,"outputTokens":21583,"cacheReadInputTokens":3817817,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59691,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2184294000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2647,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":88,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Deployed PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (initial primary), node2, node3 (standbys) on RHEL 10, generating the replicator credential on node1 and distributing it node-to-node over SSH (never printed). Verified live replication, then exercised failover: stopped node1, promoted node2 to writable primary with zero committed-data loss, reparented node3 to stream from node2, and re-provisioned node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart protocol on all three nodes (node1, node3, then primary node2 last), proving changed OS boot IDs and full PostgreSQL/replication recovery (including node2 correctly resuming as primary and both standbys auto-reattaching) after each restart, with a final end-to-end write replicated to both standbys.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed postgresql-server 16.14 on node1, node2, node3\",\"Initialized primary DB on node1, configured wal_level/replica settings and pg_hba.conf for replication\",\"Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes\",\"Generated replicator role password on node1 via /dev/urandom (never printed) and created the replication role without exposing the password in output\",\"Distributed the password to node2/node3 over cluster SSH keys, avoiding literal secrets in commands\",\"Cloned node2 and node3 as standbys of node1 via pg_basebackup -R, created physical replication slots, started replication, verified streaming state and replicated a test table\",\"Captured pre-failover committed data and confirmed it was present on both standbys\",\"Simulated primary loss by stopping postgresql on node1; promoted node2 via pg_promote() with zero committed-data loss (rows 1-2 intact) and confirmed a new write succeeded\",\"Reparented node3 to stream from node2 (updated primary_conninfo/primary_slot_name, verified streaming state)\",\"Rebuilt node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup and confirmed it rejoined with full data including post-failover writes\",\"Verified full 3-node topology (node2 primary, node1+node3 standbys) with a final committed write replicated to both standbys\",\"Captured per-node boot_id and postgres/replication health baseline\",\"Restarted node1, node3, then node2 (the primary, restarted last) one at a time via systemctl reboot with background-launched command so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled each node's exec availability post-restart and confirmed changed boot_id after each restart\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: node1 and node3 rejoined as standbys with all historical data, node2 resumed correctly as primary (not standby) with both standbys auto-reattached\",\"Performed a final end-to-end write on node2 and confirmed replication to node1 and node3 after all restarts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-node streaming replication established, node1 primary writable, node2/node3 standbys\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-16e3a4eea6834efd\",\"cmd-73b10e5b29fb4271\",\"cmd-b7726db4b8524795\",\"cmd-5f41ce9c526f4a96\",\"cmd-fc321a5734754321\",\"cmd-554311ebed4b47ad\",\"cmd-2d4a424820034919\"],\"summary\":\"Postgres started on node1, node2/node3 base-backed up from node1 with -R, pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys streaming via active physical slots, and a test row inserted on node1 replicated to both standbys with pg_is_in_recovery=true on each\"},{\"requirement\":\"Credentials generated on managed nodes, not exposed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7e1cab8d417749ab\",\"cmd-bf0385de9723414e\"],\"summary\":\"Replicator password generated via /dev/urandom directly on node1 filesystem and consumed server-side by psql variable substitution; role created without the password ever appearing in command args or output\"},{\"requirement\":\"Failover: standby takes over as writable primary without losing committed data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1ae705ae8f144528\",\"cmd-6d93132713e5473d\",\"cmd-85704c49b72b44ca\",\"cmd-7c631b08e5eb42f2\",\"cmd-d18326ce189d4059\",\"cmd-dd5d90f669174b22\"],\"summary\":\"Committed row 'pre-failover-committed' verified present on both standbys before disruption; node1 postgres stopped; node2 promoted via pg_promote() to pg_is_in_recovery=false; post-promotion query shows rows 1 and 2 intact plus a new write, proving no data loss\"},{\"requirement\":\"Surviving standby re-parented to new primary during failover\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-575b49eb77c94cb3\",\"cmd-61d9aa9e9e6544b7\",\"cmd-dcc79f9ec3214a4f\",\"cmd-e04ad83d17b1433a\"],\"summary\":\"node3 primary_conninfo repointed from node1 to node2, restarted, confirmed streaming to node2 (pg_stat_replication) and pg_is_in_recovery=true with post-failover data present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Recovered former primary rejoins as standby of the new primary\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0d844eecb5144d6e\",\"cmd-1dbcc19199be4b77\",\"cmd-3eeb5d71f0ee4a0b\",\"cmd-46fbe9bba6204c1e\",\"cmd-5e3c9f9f278a4a4c\",\"cmd-d78c55b069924e12\"],\"summary\":\"node1 re-cloned via pg_basebackup from node2, started as standby (pg_is_in_recovery=true) with all historical and post-failover data; node2 pg_stat_replication shows both node1 and node3 streaming with active slots; a final cluster-wide write replicated to both\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-83854c010e004f8f\",\"cmd-249f96d7c1594693\",\"cmd-9c1fd33a70ae4441\",\"cmd-b1aef2f773de478d\",\"cmd-22aff0a2fbbc4acd\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6ab6a71b captured with postgres active/standby-healthy; systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to ed875a28 after reconnect; postgres active, standby recovery confirmed with all data; node2 shows node1 reattached to replication\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b0e91f3e20e84f36\",\"cmd-ddf17193ce4a4f5e\",\"cmd-526353b0bcb8442a\",\"cmd-a11c462c5028405e\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 19062a82 captured; reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed to bbd64094 after reconnect; postgres active, standby recovery confirmed with all data intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node2 (primary) restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state as primary with quorum\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-09d2c62827c542cd\",\"cmd-913021f763d340c6\",\"cmd-34bdede687a443e0\",\"cmd-d7b80a255b664bd9\",\"cmd-1ca9bef314024442\",\"cmd-bb0dfdece7ce48e1\",\"cmd-6f0f82b86e5b4556\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 03408ac4 captured with node2 as writable primary and 2 streaming replicas; reboot acknowledged (restarted last, after node1/node3 quorum confirmed healthy); boot_id changed to df7ca49a after reconnect; node2 resumed correctly as primary (not standby) with both standbys auto-reattached; final write replicated to both node1 and node3\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed PostgreSQL 16 streaming replication across node1 (initial primary), node2, node3 (standbys) on RHEL 10, generating the replicator credential on node1 and distributing it node-to-node over SSH (never printed). Verified live replication, then exercised failover: stopped node1, promoted node2 to writable primary with zero committed-data loss, reparented node3 to stream from node2, and re-provisioned node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart protocol on all three nodes (node1, node3, then primary node2 last), proving changed OS boot IDs and full PostgreSQL/replication recovery (including node2 correctly resuming as primary and both standbys auto-reattaching) after each restart, with a final end-to-end write replicated to both standbys.","actions_performed":["Installed postgresql-server 16.14 on node1, node2, node3","Initialized primary DB on node1, configured wal_level/replica settings and pg_hba.conf for replication","Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes","Generated replicator role password on node1 via /dev/urandom (never printed) and created the replication role without exposing the password in output","Distributed the password to node2/node3 over cluster SSH keys, avoiding literal secrets in commands","Cloned node2 and node3 as standbys of node1 via pg_basebackup -R, created physical replication slots, started replication, verified streaming state and replicated a test table","Captured pre-failover committed data and confirmed it was present on both standbys","Simulated primary loss by stopping postgresql on node1; promoted node2 via pg_promote() with zero committed-data loss (rows 1-2 intact) and confirmed a new write succeeded","Reparented node3 to stream from node2 (updated primary_conninfo/primary_slot_name, verified streaming state)","Rebuilt node1 as a standby of node2 via pg_basebackup and confirmed it rejoined with full data including post-failover writes","Verified full 3-node topology (node2 primary, node1+node3 standbys) with a final committed write replicated to both standbys","Captured per-node boot_id and postgres/replication health baseline","Restarted node1, node3, then node2 (the primary, restarted last) one at a time via systemctl reboot with background-launched command so acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled each node's exec availability post-restart and confirmed changed boot_id after each restart","Verified post-restart recovery: node1 and node3 rejoined as standbys with all historical data, node2 resumed correctly as primary (not standby) with both standbys auto-reattached","Performed a final end-to-end write on node2 and confirmed replication to node1 and node3 after all restarts"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-node streaming replication established, node1 primary writable, node2/node3 standbys","command_ids":["cmd-16e3a4eea6834efd","cmd-73b10e5b29fb4271","cmd-b7726db4b8524795","cmd-5f41ce9c526f4a96","cmd-fc321a5734754321","cmd-554311ebed4b47ad","cmd-2d4a424820034919"],"summary":"Postgres started on node1, node2/node3 base-backed up from node1 with -R, pg_stat_replication on node1 shows both standbys streaming via active physical slots, and a test row inserted on node1 replicated to both standbys with pg_is_in_recovery=true on each"},{"requirement":"Credentials generated on managed nodes, not exposed","command_ids":["cmd-7e1cab8d417749ab","cmd-bf0385de9723414e"],"summary":"Replicator password generated via /dev/urandom directly on node1 filesystem and consumed server-side by psql variable substitution; role created without the password ever appearing in command args or output"},{"requirement":"Failover: standby takes over as writable primary without losing committed data","command_ids":["cmd-1ae705ae8f144528","cmd-6d93132713e5473d","cmd-85704c49b72b44ca","cmd-7c631b08e5eb42f2","cmd-d18326ce189d4059","cmd-dd5d90f669174b22"],"summary":"Committed row 'pre-failover-committed' verified present on both standbys before disruption; node1 postgres stopped; node2 promoted via pg_promote() to pg_is_in_recovery=false; post-promotion query shows rows 1 and 2 intact plus a new write, proving no data loss"},{"requirement":"Surviving standby re-parented to new primary during failover","command_ids":["cmd-575b49eb77c94cb3","cmd-61d9aa9e9e6544b7","cmd-dcc79f9ec3214a4f","cmd-e04ad83d17b1433a"],"summary":"node3 primary_conninfo repointed from node1 to node2, restarted, confirmed streaming to node2 (pg_stat_replication) and pg_is_in_recovery=true with post-failover data present"},{"requirement":"Recovered former primary rejoins as standby of the new primary","command_ids":["cmd-0d844eecb5144d6e","cmd-1dbcc19199be4b77","cmd-3eeb5d71f0ee4a0b","cmd-46fbe9bba6204c1e","cmd-5e3c9f9f278a4a4c","cmd-d78c55b069924e12"],"summary":"node1 re-cloned via pg_basebackup from node2, started as standby (pg_is_in_recovery=true) with all historical and post-failover data; node2 pg_stat_replication shows both node1 and node3 streaming with active slots; a final cluster-wide write replicated to both"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state","comman